### T-Shop API walkthrough
### Run the requests in order with the VS Code "REST Client" extension (or IntelliJ's HTTP client,
### adapting the token capture). Start the app first: ./mvnw spring-boot:run

@baseUrl = http://localhost:9000/api/v1

### 1. Browse the catalogue (public)
GET {{baseUrl}}/products?q=dell&sort=price_asc

### 2. Log in as the demo customer
# @name customerLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "test@test.test", "password": "test"}

### 3. Add an address
@customerToken = {{customerLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
# @name address
POST {{baseUrl}}/me/addresses
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"country": "Spain", "postalCode": "28001", "street": "Gran Via", "houseNumber": "1"}

### 4. Put two units of product 1 in the cart
PUT {{baseUrl}}/me/cart/items/1
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"quantity": 2}

### 5. See the cart
GET {{baseUrl}}/me/cart
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### 6. Place the order
# @name order
POST {{baseUrl}}/me/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"addressId": {{address.response.body.id}}, "paymentMethod": "CARD", "deliveryMethod": "STANDARD"}

### 7. Log in as admin
# @name adminLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "admin@admin.admin", "password": "admin"}

### 8. Confirm the order (the card payment becomes PAID)
@adminToken = {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
PUT {{baseUrl}}/admin/orders/{{order.response.body.id}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"status": "CONFIRMED"}

### 9. The customer sees the new status
GET {{baseUrl}}/me/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### 10. A customer can't use admin endpoints (403)
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/customers
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
